From dsmith at statsci.com  Thu Jun  1 17:18:44 2000
From: dsmith at statsci.com (David M Smith)
Date: Thu, 01 Jun 2000 10:18:44 -0700
Subject: [S] S-PLUS, Windows 2000 and Office 2000
In-Reply-To: <3935EEF038A.EE72SGSONG@smtp.ben2.ucla.edu>
References: <3935EEF038A.EE72SGSONG@smtp.ben2.ucla.edu>
Message-ID: <005101bfcbed$70cd65a0$180110ac@statsci.com>

This is the current and planned support status for S-PLUS with Windows 2000
and Office 2000.

Windows 2000
============

Windows 2000 is NOT supported for any currently-released versions of S-PLUS
2000. However, S-PLUS 2000 R2 has been tested on Windows 2000, and is known
to run.  There are several known minor issues with Windows 2000, most of
which have simple workarounds:

* You cannot export objects with periods in column names via ODBC.  The
workaround is to rename the object, e.g., rename fuel.frame to fuelframe

* Client installations of S-PLUS 2000 for Windows Networks fail to obtain a
license unless S_ELMHOST is specified on the Target line of the shortcut
icon.  (See  http://www.splus.mathsoft.com/splus/splssupport/ for the
workaround)

* There are problems with the function objdiff().

MathSoft will shortly release a patch -- S-PLUS 2000 Release 3 -- which will
fully support Windows 2000 by resolving these issues.  There will be no new
features included in the patch.

Office 2000
===========

Office 2000 has been tested with S-PLUS 2000 R2, and is supported on Windows
95, Windows 98 and NT 4.0 Service Pack 3 or later.  S-PLUS 2000 Release 3
will support Office 2000 under Windows 2000.

