I'm having trouble with what I'm sure is a very simple problem, i.e.,
specifying the correct syntax for a simple split plot design. To check
my understanding I'm using the cake data set from Table 7.5 of Cochran
& Cox.  For those of you who don't have a copy handy, the data is
structured as follows:

   Three different cake recipes were tested.
   Each time a recipe was prepared, enough was made to bake the cake
     at six different temperatures.
   There were fifteen replications for each of the cake recipes.
   The response variable is the angle at which the cake broke when one
     half was fixed and one half was pivoted.

So recipes are the whole-plot unit and baking temperatures are the
sub-plot unit. I've transcribed the data and imported it into a
dataframe 

   > summary(splitplot)
    recipe  temperature    replicate       angle      
    1:90   Min.   :175   15     : 18   Min.   :18.00  
    2:90   1st Qu.:185   14     : 18   1st Qu.:26.00  
    3:90   Median :200   13     : 18   Median :31.00  
           Mean   :200   12     : 18   Mean   :32.12  
           3rd Qu.:215   11     : 18   3rd Qu.:36.75  
           Max.   :225   10     : 18   Max.   :63.00  
                         (Other):162            

My problem is in specifying the error term, and it's probably as
simple as not understanding what the error term really is. The ANOVA
table Cochran & Cox present is structured like this:

    Source                    d.f.
    ------                    ----
Whole-plot
    Replications                14
    Recipes                      1
    Error                       28
Sub-plot
    Temperatures                 5
    Recipes x temperatures      10
    Error                      210

The closest I've come to replicating this is

   > splitplot.recipes <- aov(angle ~ recipe*as.factor(temperature)
   + + Error(replicate), splitplot)
   > summary(splitplot.recipes)
   
   Error: replicate
                          Df Sum Sq Mean Sq F value Pr(>F)
   as.factor(temperature)  1  585.8   585.8  0.7917 0.3898
   Residuals              13 9618.5   739.9               
   
   Error: Within
                                  Df Sum Sq Mean Sq F value    Pr(>F)    
   recipe                          2  135.1    67.5  2.9225   0.05573 .  
   as.factor(temperature)          5 2093.1   418.6 18.1124 3.220e-15 ***
   recipe:as.factor(temperature)  10  209.9    21.0  0.9082   0.52626    
   Residuals                     238 5500.7    23.1                      

The total SS from "Error: replicate" corresponds to C&C's whole-plot
"Replications" and the SS from "recipe" corresponds to C&C's
whole-plot "Recipes", but I can't figure out what error term I need to
specify to match C&C's results. Surely I'm missing something simple,
but I've been staring at this for two hours, and I haven't been able
to figure out the answer yet.

