If MatrixA is of class "Matrix" then by invoking
library(matrix) you are using either eigen.Matrix()
or eigen.Hermitian() when you say eigen(MatrixA).
I couldn't find a claim that the eigenvalues were
in descending order in the help files for either
of these functions. However, the help file for
function eigen.default(), which is used for matrices
that
are not of class "Matrix", does say that the
eigenvalues are in descending order.

Regards,

Mirka

(PS It looks like MatrixA is symmetric so you probably
want it to be of class "Hermitian" in addition to
"Matrix" if it isn't already in order to take
advantage
of the symmetric eigenvalue decomposition.)

