Yes, the Error() term can be a bit frustrating, but not nearly as
frustrating as trying to figure out exactly what kind of analysis the C & C
actually did. Once that is done, the following gives the same results as
C&C, without the further breakdown of the Temperatures SS into regression
and residual. In fact, the summary even gives the results in the same order,
which trumps Minitab :-)

cake.data$Temp <- factor(cake.data$temp)
cake.data$Rep  <- factor(cake.data$replic)
cake.data$Recipe <- factor(cake.data$recipe)

summary(aov(br.angle ~ Recipe*Temp + Error(Rep/Recipe), data=cake.data))

The trick is to figure out just what C&C are using as plots and subplots,
and what is nested in what.  BTW, Greg,  that's v. hard to do without the
book itself.

