On Mon, 5 Jun 2000, Aldi Kraja wrote:

> By the way, you mentioned the 3.* versions. I am using Splus v5.*, but I
> return to 3.4 version for unix, to use "rpart" functions. Do you know if
> there is any version of "rpart" that works with newer versions of Splus?

Yes, of course.  The latest rpart(2) has only been released for 5.x,
although I back-ported it for 2000.  See http://www.mayo.edu/hsr/Sfunc.html
for the sources.

There is not much that does not work under 5.1.  The only exception I know
of is lspec, and that is basically due to illegal C calls.  Often a little
tweaking is needed, or a lot for nlme, for example (but that has been done:
see nlme.stat.wisc.edu).

