> 
> A point that may interest some readers is that S-Plus and R don't
> summarize the model in quite the same way. Given the C&C data and the

[...]

> Does R not recognize the split() syntax in this context? I couldn't
> find anything about it in the manuals.

Exactly. There is nothing about it in the R manuals.  (It is nothing to do
with split(), by the way, just an argument called split to
summary.aovlist.)  R, like S-PLUS, does not generally document the absence
of features it has never had!  (If you think it should, R-devel not S-news
is the place to discuss it.)

My own take on this is that if you want to see tables for the
components of an aov term, you should specify the model using the
terms you want to see the answer for.  So the split argument to
summary.aovlist seems pretty unnatural to me.  Since we no
longer walk 500m to the computer centre to enter data on punched cards,
(at least I don't)  we don't need all possible information in the 
printout and can refine the model interactively.

