From: rdiazuri at students.wisc.edu (Ramon Diaz-Uriarte)
Date: Thu, 08 Jun 2000 10:09:12 +0200
Subject: [S] coxph with frailty terms: df's for LR tests
Message-ID: <00060810135903.00354@ligarto>

Dear All,

I have some coxph models with frailty terms. These are nested models, and I
often want to test for one or more factor terms with more than two levels. I
thought the way to go was to use likelihood ratio tests, but I am not
sure I am doing it right. First, I am not sure what d.f.'s I should use: the
number of levels -1, or the difference in df's from the fitted models. Second,
sometimes the likelihood ratio is very different from what I expected (even
with negative sign!).

Here are some examples:

kfit1 <- coxph(Surv(time,status) ~ age + sex + disease + frailty(id), 
data=kidney)
kfit2 <- coxph(Surv(time,status) ~ age + sex + frailty(id), data=kidney)
kfit3 <- coxph(Surv(time,status) ~ age + disease + frailty(id), data=kidney)

## sex, with LR test of nested models:
-2 * (kfit3$loglik[2] - kfit1$loglik[2]) # chi-square not the same as from kfit1

## disease, with LR of nested models
-2 * (kfit2$loglik[2] - kfit1$loglik[2]) # chi-square; it is negative!
# and what df's:
sum(kfit1$df) - sum(kfit2$df) # = (-9.14) or 3?

What is the right way of dealing with this?

Thanks

-- 
