Message-ID: <Pine.GSO.4.05.10006090603370.4420-100000@auk.stats>

On Thu, 8 Jun 2000, Paul Schwarz wrote:

> 
> Hi S-news readers:
> 
> I'm looking for an easy way to calculate standardized regression
> coefficients for a regression model e.g., either lm() or glm().  By
> standardized, I mean:
> 
> Bi = bi * sqrt(sum(xi)/sum(yi))

Surely you mean the sum of squares about the mean here?  Or at least a 
sum of squares?

> I can't think of a way to select only the xi's used in the model.

The easy way is to scale the data. If all your terms are in data1 and you
used lm(y ~ ., data1), try

data2 <- lapply(data1, scale)
lm(y ~ ., data2)

and if you really mean the scaling you suggest, replace this by

data2 <- lapply(data1, function(x) x/sqrt(mean(x)))

