clutter let me define a utility function that takes a model formula
and prints out its terms.

  > m <- function(form) labels(terms(form))

Now

  > m(y ~ d / (a + b + c))
  [1] "d"        "a %in% d" "b %in% d" "c %in% d"

This is as I expected.  Note that a term like "a %in% d" is the same
thing as "a:d" so that all of a, b, and c interact with d.

However if I specify 2nd order interactions among the a, b, and c I
