Message-ID: <001501bfd51b$8fa8c960$07c809c0@pcjmw>

hello,

> 2) I also want to filter lists into a property on a dialog. There is a
> function to do this for data frames ( I think TX-PROP_dataframes). This
> does not work on list, however. Any ideas?

suppose you have a property called MyfuncList, defined like this :
guiCreate( "Property", Name = "MyfuncList",
 Type = "Normal",
 DialogPrompt = "Li$sts :",
 DialogControl = "Combo Box",
 )

You can do a (basic) callback function for your purpose :

backMyfunc <- function(data){
 #selection of list objects
 LISTS <- unlist(lapply(objects(),function(x){bool <- is.list(get(x));

bool[is.na(bool)]<-F;return(bool)}))
#format the list
 list.x <- paste(objects()[LISTS],collapse=",")
#display the items in the combo box
 data <- cbSetOptionList(data,"MyfuncList",list.x)
 data
}

You can customize a bit more the callback function : all this stuff has not
to be done each time a button is used, doing it when the dialog box is first
launched may be enough.
Even if all this is not very optimized, it works fine...

hope this helps, regards,

    Mathieu Ros

