moving a function of mine from Splus 3.3 to Splus 2000 I receive an error
message (i.e.: Error in seq.default: Missing value where logical needed:
if(from == to || length.out < 2) by <- 1) during the execution of the 
line

   stime <- merge( stime, temp, by=1, all=T )

in the following piece of program:

...
fit <- survfit( Surv( lung$time, lung$status ) ~ lung$sex )
stime <- data.frame( time = sort( unique( fit$time ) ) )
nstrat <- length( fit$strata )
stemp <- rep( 1:nstrat, fit$strata )
for( i in unique( stemp ) ) {
   who <- ( stemp == i )
   temp <- data.frame( fit$time[who], fit$n.risk[who], fit$n.event[who] )
   stime <- merge( stime, temp, by=1, all=T )
}
