The easiest way to get (X'X)^{-1} from lm is to access the R matrix from the
QR decomposition, which is (in your setup) out$R.  Setting Rinv<-solve(out$R),
you have
(X'X)^{-1} = Rinv %*% t(Rinv).

Joseph F.  Lucke
Statistician, Center for Nursing Research
University of Pittsburgh

