The reason why I stick to glm for discriminant analysis is that number of
observation (i.e., number of data) is sometimes different group to group.
Fisher's Iris data contained data obtained from 4 measurements on 50
flowers from each of 3 species of iris.  My data correspond to a case when
only 40 floweres were used for measurement in some of 3 species of iris.
To solve this problem, to my knowledge, glm should be used.  If this is not 
correct understanding, please point it out.  If lda can treat such data as
mine, I will use lda.

