Two disadvantages of that approach is that with jpeg/png some resolution
might be lost and that conversion to Microsoft word would not work as
well as with RTF.  But one of the disadvantages of the RTFf approach is that
it is easy to distort the aspect ratio of the graphics, and when the
graphics are converted to Word some special features are lost.
In my experience postscript is the most faithful format, so what I
would like to see is a report window that looks as it does now but
that instead of embedding graphics has links to external postscript
files.  If an import to Word would use that, even better (but I
use LaTeX anyway).  -Frank Harrell

