I have received contradictory advice on how to use LateX on Windows.
In the summary I am not including all the responses, just the more common
ones.

- some people preferred MiKTeX others fpTeX
- for editors some people preferred WinEdt, other Emacs + AUC-TEX, others PFE.
- some people reccomended getting GSview, while others did not find it necessary
because MiKTeX allows them to preview .dvi files.

It seems like the simplest set-up is WinEdt + MiKTeX, although some of the
other configurations may have some benefits, especially for the S-Plus user
who may want to use the S-Plus interface of Emacs.

